WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:01.680
Hey, David.

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:06.029
I like most of Bernie's policies, but I don't
like burning everyone.

00:00:06.029 --> 00:00:09.560
I know that has met
him, I says, he's a dick.

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:11.230
Okay, I wonder who you know that as matter.

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:16.400
I also don't want a nearly 80 year old leading
the Progressive Movement.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:19.420
He has to stop saying he's
a democratic socialist.

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:20.890
It'll never work.

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:24.610
Does the Progressive Movement need a re­brand?

00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:31.570
Your question implies a sort of similar understanding
to some of the analysis I made after Super

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:36.600
Tuesday, and what that analysis was included.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:40.059
The realization that something like Medicare
for All

00:00:40.059 --> 00:00:44.050
the left is split on Medicare for all.

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:46.170
You have people who simply don't want it...

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:49.000
You have people
who do want it, but not at the exclusion of

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.840
being able to keep private insurance.

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:52.791
There's a lot of
different opinions about Medicare for all

00:00:52.791 --> 00:00:54.059
on the left.

00:00:54.059 --> 00:01:01.820
My belief is that many elements 75, 80% of
Medicare, for all most of the Left would come

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:05.580
around
to, if it was given to them by the right candidate

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:10.840
and framed in the right way and not presented
as

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:14.750
what you have will be taken away, but rather
this will be created and you can choose to

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:17.229
take
advantage of this or if you wanna keep paying

00:01:17.229 --> 00:01:19.020
for insurance, you can do it.

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:21.409
But we are going to
fund this in the following way, as Bernie

00:01:21.409 --> 00:01:22.409
is pointed out.

00:01:22.409 --> 00:01:23.619
Okay, in a...

00:01:23.619 --> 00:01:29.590
I don't think it's crazy to say that when
you hear it from a nearly 80 year old Democratic

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:34.770
Socialist
from Brooklyn, if you are a North Florida

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:37.470
Democrat, you were more likely to be repelled
by it than

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:38.710
to welcome in.

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:45.640
This is not my view understand, I don't care
about Bernie's identity, and I'm doing

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:51.520
the best that I can to look at the policies,
but I understand that there are a lot of people

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:55.009
who would
be in favor of 80% of bones, Medicare for

00:01:55.009 --> 00:01:56.220
All plan.

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:58.409
And is free college plan, assuming that it's
the

00:01:58.409 --> 00:02:00.549
version that includes trade school, and so
on.

00:02:00.549 --> 00:02:06.549
The policies themselves are certainly more
popular than it might appear from the overwhelming

00:02:06.549 --> 00:02:11.160
way, in which Joe Biden has outperformed Bernie
in the popular vote in the Democratic primary.

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:12.160
