00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:14.680
So, yeah, I completely understand what you're
saying now, as far as whether the progressive

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:18.269
movement needs to re­brand, I'm less sure
about that.

00:02:18.269 --> 00:02:20.810
One of the concerns I've expressed is when
I

00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:24.480
see people defying politicians almost like...

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:27.769
Like God, like deities I don't care who it
is.

00:02:27.769 --> 00:02:29.879
I think that
that's a problem, right?

00:02:29.879 --> 00:02:37.210
You have a movement in this country it's probably
about 60 or 70% of Trump supporters that see

00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:38.450
Trump as a pseudo­deity.

00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:41.659
They see him almost like a God, He can do
no wrong, he can shoot

00:02:41.659 --> 00:02:43.749
someone on Fifth Avenue whatever.

00:02:43.749 --> 00:02:45.700
I think that that's absolutely terrible.

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:48.579
I've pointed out before,
there are elements of this in the Democratic

00:02:48.579 --> 00:02:50.409
Party as well.

00:02:50.409 --> 00:02:55.940
I would say anecdotally, from the emails
I got I had tools, supporters Andrew Yang

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:58.839
supporters and Bernie supporters who really
seemed to

00:02:58.839 --> 00:03:06.579
see the three respective candidates, as almost
perfect beings as almost they are defying

00:03:06.579 --> 00:03:08.060
them in
some way.

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:11.670
And I don't know if it's because I've met
enough of these politicians that I just don't

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:14.889
get sucked into
the cult of personality or whatever, but these

00:03:14.889 --> 00:03:17.400
are just people, these are flawed people,
they all have

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:21.180
some good ideas and some ideas that are not
so good, you can like nine out of 10 policies

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:24.069
from one
person and you can still recognize maybe that

00:03:24.069 --> 00:03:26.589
10th out of 10 policy doesn't make sense.

00:03:26.589 --> 00:03:28.860
Or does the
numbers don't balance or whatever the case

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:29.860
may be?

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:33.049
And when I see anyone defying a candidate,
I

00:03:33.049 --> 00:03:37.030
get concerned because I don't think that we
should be defying politicians at all.

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:41.790
There's a very emotional reaction to Bernie
among some of the supporters that reminds

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:44.729
me of some
of the emotional reaction that we see with

00:03:44.729 --> 00:03:47.659
Donald Trump and I remember I support the
vast

00:03:47.659 --> 00:03:51.670
majority of Bernie's policies and we've been
supporting him on the program for a while.

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:57.019
That doesn't mean that I see Bernie as the
blend, all in terms of the Progressive Movement,

00:03:57.019 --> 00:03:59.370
I think
that the way that the progressive movement

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:04.099
will succeed is not necessarily a re­brand,
but it's

00:04:04.099 --> 00:04:05.290
number one.

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:07.449
You gotta stop the Democratic Socialist stuff.

00:04:07.449 --> 00:04:09.900
I've been talking about that for a very,
very long time.

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:13.809
I know there's part of the Progressive Movement
that likes to say socialism pulls

00:04:13.809 --> 00:04:15.650
better than it has in decades.

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:20.269
It still doesn't pull that well, and it's
still not a good idea to be talking

00:04:20.269 --> 00:04:24.900
about when the policies you're advocating
aren't actually democratic socialist policies,

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:26.000
there's no
upside.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:30.850
So whether it's a rebrand or whether it's
picking candidates that may be better relate

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:33.020
to
people demographically or whatever the case,

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:34.020
my...

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:35.020
Is it AOC.

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:36.300
I don't know, maybe...

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:38.570
Maybe not, I
don't know, does she call herself a democratic

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:39.570
socialist?

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:42.409
I'm not sure but what you have to look at
is

00:04:42.409 --> 00:04:44.139
in a way, it's crazy.

00:04:44.139 --> 00:04:50.090
Look at what the Tea Party did in 2010, the
Tea Party with terrible policies that

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:55.330
were genuinely back for the vast majority
of the people that supported the party candidates

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:58.440
built a
pseudo Movement, which was then integrated

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:01.599
into the Republican Party, and move the entire
party

00:05:01.599 --> 00:05:03.200
in that direction.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:07.110
You're not seeing that happen in the same
way with the progressive movement.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:10.190
And I don't know, it
pains me to see it not happen.

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:15.570
I don't know if it's the people, I don't believe
that it's the policies, I think the policies

00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:19.050
are good, it
may be the framing or the language around

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:20.050
some of the policies.

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:23.330
I'm going to be thinking about this
a lot and talking about it at once we get

00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:25.669
past the primary phase, but I'd be curious
to hear from you,

00:05:25.669 --> 00:05:25.671
for sure.

